the balance between cost,

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:59.110
complexity, scale,
and utilization.

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:00.130
LILIANA YU: Absolutely.

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:02.650
When I've got vast quantities
of data to process,

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:05.050
I want to be focusing on
the insights provided,

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:06.910
not the cluster processing it.

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:09.370
As a managed Spark and
Hadoop cloud service,

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:12.100
Cloud Dataproc makes
these powerful data tools

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.372
easy to use.

00:01:13.372 --> 00:01:15.580
SAMAN JAVAN: What you don't
want to be worrying about

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:18.747
in data processing is
cost and complexity.

00:01:18.747 --> 00:01:20.830
LILIANA YU: Using Spark
and Hadoop shouldn't break

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:24.360
the bank, so on top of the
other GCP resources you use,

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:27.740
there's only a small incremental
fee payable per virtual CPU

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:28.930
in your cluster.

00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:31.660
Dataproc automation also
helps you save money

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:34.660
by turning clusters off
when you don't need them.

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.550
With billing in one
second clock time

00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:38.920
increments, subject
to one minute minimum,

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:40.930
you also only pay
for what you use.

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:48.070
